    {
      "code": "cyclic_navigation",
      "detail": "5 of the 13 navigations lead back to somewhere they came from, so the back stack can grow past the number of destinations the reader has visited. 1 of those 5 already replace rather than push (`popUpTo` + `launchSingleTop`); the rest are drill-downs and deliberate switches, so this is a number to watch rather than a defect.",
      "severity": "info",
      "site": null,
      "subject": "graph",
      "title": "5 navigation edges close a loop"
    },
    {
      "code": "terminal_destination",
      "detail": "Every screen it renders is a leaf of the navigation graph: there is no `navigate` call inside it. Expected for a detail screen, wrong for anything meant to be a hub.",
